# Sherlock Holmes, Local mode only. bin/compose-agents.sh reads this file; the
# format is in that script's header.
name: holmes-local
source: holmes
description: Sherlock Holmes in Local mode only — a six-slot brief in, a prose verdict on the uncommitted working tree out, with no Index call and no GitHub write. Dispatch workbench-dev-team:holmes, which routes a brief here.
tools: Agent, Bash, Read, Grep, Glob, mcp__plugin_workbench-core_memory__read, mcp__plugin_workbench-core_memory__write, mcp__plugin_workbench-core_memory__edit, mcp__plugin_workbench-core_memory__search

requires: Agent, Bash, Read, Grep, Glob

section: # Sherlock Holmes — Code Review Agent
section: ## How you write
section: ## When a gate or guard refuses you
section: ## Scratch folders — a bare `mktemp`, deleted when your run ends
section: ## Validation — run the tests in place, and inspect them
skip: ## Mode detection
skip: ## The Index-mode input contract
section: ## The brief contract — refuse an incomplete brief, ask about a vague one
section: ## Working-context budget — roughly 250k tokens, self-checked
section: ## Tools
skip: ## Tools — The Index mode
section: ## Local mode
skip: ## The Index-mode workflow
text: ## The steps Local mode shares with The Index mode
text:
text: `references/holmes/local-review.md` names each step below by its Index-mode
text: number and says how it applies to a local review. The other Index-mode steps
text: are not yours.
section: ### 0. The config line (fan-out knobs)
skip: ### 1. Fetch the item
skip: ### 2. Find the PR
skip: ### 2.5. Decision request? (answer mode — before reviewing code)
skip: ### 3. Compute the strike count — informs §5, never skips the review
skip: ### 4. Review the PR
skip: #### Phase A — set up the evidence
skip: ##### 4a. Read the issue and AC
section: ##### 4a.5. Search `feedback/` before you judge — required, in both modes
skip: ##### 4b. Check out the PR — the shared evidence room
skip: ##### 4c. Confirm the tests passed — trust CI, don't re-run
section: #### Phases B, C, and D — fan-out, adversarial verification, memory context
section: #### 4d. Check conformance against the acceptance criteria — the contract
section: #### 4e. Defects and observations beyond the AC — route by the coherent unit of work, then coupling and locality
skip: ### 5. Submit your verdict — three outcomes, and only three
skip: #### 🕰️ Before you write anything — re-read the item
skip: #### ✅ APPROVE — every AC item met, no hard defect this repo can fix, and the PR's own code **plus everything belonging to the coherent unit** carry no actionable finding
skip: #### 🔄 REQUEST CHANGES — an AC item is unmet (impl wrong/incomplete), a hard defect surfaced, or the PR's own code **or anything belonging to the coherent unit** carries an actionable finding
skip: #### 🛑 ESCALATE — the **AC itself** looks wrong/imprecise/impossible/contradicted, **or** the impl diverges from an AC item in a way you can't confidently call a strict, nothing-dropped improvement
skip: ### 5.5. Record review learnings — on every verdict
skip: ### 6. Report
section: ## Rules
section: ## Rules — Local mode
skip: ## Rules — The Index mode

cut: The Index-mode PR checkout (step 4b) is the one exception: your helpers read it
cut: Workdir: <absolute path, plus the branch or worktree when one was agreed>
cut: **You never create one and never switch to one.**
put: Confirm which branch or worktree you are in, review the tree as you find it, and say plainly in your verdict when it is not the one `Workdir:` named. The mechanics are §L4b of the Local-mode reference.
cut: All six slots are required.
cut: **A brief missing a required slot is not work you start.**
cut: **Two fixed-token shapes are exempt from both rules.**
cut: **Your own fan-out is exempt as well.**
cut: - `Bash` — clone + reads to review the code:
put: - `Bash` — reads of the local tree, and the repo's own test suite. The review guard refuses every `gh` write verb, `curl`, `security`, and every write outside the scratch roots, for you and every helper.
cut: No GraphQL, no curl, no Keychain lookups.
cut: **Every `mcp__the-index__` tool is The Index mode's alone.**
cut: Three limits define the mode, and none of them is negotiable.
put: Code holds the three limits of the mode, for you and every helper you dispatch: you hold no `mcp__the-index__` tool, the review guard refuses every GitHub write, and it refuses every write to the tree outside the scratch roots, so git is read-only here. Your verdict goes to the session that dispatched you, as prose.
cut: - **No `mcp__the-index__` call of any kind.**
cut: - **No GitHub write of any kind**
cut: - **No write to the tree.**
cut: - **Never merge PRs.**
cut: - **No Write/Edit tools — for you or your sub-agents.**
cut: - **No WebFetch.**
cut: - **Local mode writes to the vault and nowhere else**
cut: - **A local review never touches `dev-team/top-lessons.md`.**
cut: Every handoff reaches you as a **brief**: six named slots, in this order.
put: Every handoff reaches you as a **brief** of six named slots: `Workdir:`, `Goal:`, `Context:`, `Constraints:`, `Acceptance:` and `Done when:`. The dev-team mod refuses a Holmes Local dispatch that lacks a slot, or whose `Context:` reads "none".
